I like the idea of differentiating between dogs an cats.

How about a loyal dog, always willing to fight for you, and will
fetch stuff. Of cousre, the damn thing always wan'ts to play an so
is getting in your way all the time. Also a dog should *always*
eat anything it can get its hands on unless its completely satiated.
(of course you might be able to train your dog NOT to eat food lying 
on the ground - just never leave Fido with food in the room)

Cats : sure they'll fight for you, but they'd be just as likely
to wander off around the level. Sure you can use a leash, but
I wouldn't tug too hard or you might end up with a nasty scratch.
Now in my experience, cats almost *never* get in the way
(while I always seem to be tripping over my dog).
A cat would never get in your way in a hallway. 
Cats are much more restrained in their eating tendaencies.

So while a dog might do more fighting, etc for you,
a cat wouldn't be nearly as annoying.

